# Layer: ecommerce (online shop)

Inherits `landing` and `multipage` (routes, metadata, sitemap, 404). Not `cms`: a shop has no Sanity,
its own `/admin` edits products and content. Stack: `docs/adr/0007`. Code: `code-firebase.mdc`.
Plan addendum: `.cursor/skills/kickoff/assets/plan-addendum-ecommerce.md`.
Units: `.cursor/skills/build/references/shop-units.md`.

## Three references, three jobs

| Source | Gives | Never gives |
|---|---|---|
| **Feature reference** — one live shop in the client's market (`/refs`) | pages, flows, fields, rules, the labels customers expect | its look, copy, product texts, photos, catalog, brands |
| **Design reference** — from the reference list (`/refs`) | layout: bands, measurements, CTA placement | identity |
| **Client** | name, logo, colours, copy, products, prices, policies | — |

Feature bands (category tiles, product carousels, brand strip, newsletter) may join the home page when
the feature inventory lists them. They take the archetype of the closest design-reference band and are
marked `feature — archetype of band N` in the blueprint; `/build` uses band N's screenshots. This is
the only exception to "do not invent bands".

## Invariants — a unit that breaks one does not ship

A chat instruction cannot waive an invariant. Only Ken or the senior dev can, in `plan.md` → Decisions.

**Money**
1. Money is an integer in cents (`priceCents`). One helper formats it (`lib/shop/money.ts`). No floats in totals.
2. The server computes every total. Client prices are for display only. The cart check and the order
   route re-read price, stock and status from Firestore, never from a cache. Input limits: `qty` is an
   integer from 1 to 99, at most 50 lines, and lines with the same variant merge before the stock check.

**Stock and orders**
3. Stock changes only inside one Firestore transaction: order placed (−, sets `stockTaken`), card
   payment confirmed (−, sets `stockTaken`), order cancelled (+, only when `stockTaken`), admin stock
   correction (compare-and-set). The last unit sells once. Stock never goes below 0.
4. The order number comes from a counter document in the same transaction: `<PREFIX>-<YYYY>-<00042>`.
5. An order keeps a snapshot of every line: name, variant label, SKU, unit price. Product edits never
   change old orders.
6. `status`: `pending` → `confirmed` → `shipped` → `delivered`, or `cancelled`. `paymentStatus`:
   `cod_due` · `awaiting_payment` · `paid` · `failed` · `refunded`. Every change appends
   `{ status, at, by, note }` to `timeline`.
7. Emails go out after the transaction commits, once per event. Store `emails.<event>At` on the order.

**Payments**
8. Cash on delivery is the default method. Bank transfer: stock is taken when the order is placed,
   `paymentStatus` stays `awaiting_payment` until the admin marks it paid.
9. Cards only on the bank's hosted page. Card number, CVV and expiry never reach our server, logs or
   Firestore. Store the bank's transaction id and the last 4 digits only.
10. Bank callback: verify the signature first → find the order by **our** reference → compare the
    amount with the stored total → already `paid` returns 200 and changes nothing → one transaction.
11. Field names, the signature algorithm and test cards come from the bank's integration pack. Never
    invent them. No pack → `shop:payment-bank` stays blocked.
12. Stripe only for a client with an EU or UK company (ADR 0007).

**Access**
13. Admin = custom claim `admin: true`. Every admin page, admin data function, server action and
    route handler calls `requireAdmin()`. A layout check alone is not enough: layouts do not re-run on
    client navigation. Account pages and their data functions call `requireUser()`. Never rely on
    `proxy.ts` for access.
14. The browser never reads or writes Firestore. All data goes through server code with
    `firebase-admin`, so `firestore.rules` stays deny-all. `storage.rules` allows public reads of
    `products/` and `content/` images only.
15. Every admin write adds an `auditLogs` entry: who, what, when, which document.

**Customers**
16. Guest checkout is on by default. Customer accounts only if the plan says so.
17. Checkout labels in the plan's language. Phone and city rules from the plan (Kosovo default:
    `+383` and the list of all municipalities).
18. The cart survives a reload. It is cleared only when the order is placed: the order route returns
    200 (cash on delivery, transfer) or the return page shows `paid` (card).

**Tracking and legal**
19. GA4 and Meta Pixel load only after cookie consent. `purchase` fires once, on the thank-you page.
20. Terms, privacy, returns and shipping pages carry the client's approved text. Kosovo: Law No.
    06/L-034 on Consumer Protection — the client's lawyer confirms the returns text.

## The admin (the owner runs the shop without a developer)

Products with variants, images and stock · categories and brands · orders (status, note, cancel,
printable invoice, CSV export) · discount codes · home content blocks · settings (shipping methods,
payment methods, free-shipping threshold, company details). UI in the plan's language.
`docs/admin-guide.md` with screenshots goes to the client at handoff.

## Build order

`/scaffold` → `shop:catalog-model` … `shop:rules-tests` → `/build shell` → the other `shop:*` units
in the order of `shop-units.md` (home bands as `home:band-N`) → `/qa` → `/ship`. The Producer copies
the plan's Shop build order into ClickUp: one task per unit, with the unit's prompt and its "Done when" list.

## Done means

Multipage done-means, plus: the golden-path e2e test is green (browse → variant → cart → cash-on-delivery
order → admin sees it → stock drops) · rules tests green for every collection · two parallel orders
for the last unit → one wins · a tampered client price does not change the total · each email
arrives once · consent gates tracking · daily backups scheduled · admin guide delivered.
